# Operational excellence (scorecard, SLOs, alerting)

Phased work and action IDs live in [docs/plans/operational-excellence.md](docs/plans/operational-excellence.md) (`OPS-*`). Treat that document as the backlog — **do not implement** PagerDuty escalate-if-unacked (`OPS-P3-002`) unless the user explicitly asks. Phase 0–3 (except `OPS-P3-002`) are done (`ALERT-*` Action Groups + living scorecard + monthly workflow + materials synthetics + field/lab FCP + Studio SLO cadence + CD Sev1 + inquiry SLI + IR stub + prod/shared KV purge protection).

## Scorecard

- Rubric lives in the plan. Living scores: `docs/ops/operational-excellence-scorecard.md` (from `docs/ops/scorecard-evaluation.json` via `scripts/ops-scorecard-refresh.mjs`).
- Monthly refresh (`OPS-P0-004`): `.github/workflows/ops-scorecard-monthly.yml` uses `scripts/mint-github-app-token.sh` (line-masked PEM), verifies Contents:write via mint response + `/installation/repositories`, and pushes with App git credentials (`persist-credentials: false`). CD ignores scorecard-only pushes. Never reintroduce `GITHUB_TOKEN` pushes, PEM `with:` inputs, or multiline `::add-mask::$PEM`.
- Scorecard content is scores, evidence, and gaps only — **never** alert emails, phones, or secrets.

## Private details never in git

When planning or implementing alerts, on-call, or support contacts:

- **Never** commit real alert emails, SMS/voice numbers, PagerDuty/Better Stack routing keys, or similar private operator details in Terraform variables files, docs, examples, canvases, PR bodies, or source comments.
- Store them in **Azure Key Vault** and read at deploy/apply time (data sources / sync scripts), same pattern as `SITE-CONTACT-*` and ACS secrets (`lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }`, set via `az keyvault secret set`).
- Use placeholders only in the repo: `REPLACE_ME`, `<email>`, `+1XXXXXXXXXX`.
- Prefer dedicated **`ALERT-*`** secrets in **`kv-elyse-shared`** (bootstrap placeholders), not reuse of `SITE-CONTACT-EMAIL` / `SITE-CONTACT-PHONE` (those are inquiry notify via ACS).
- Do **not** send ops/Sev1 alerts through ACS contact-form SMS.
- Action Groups read `ALERT-EMAIL` / `ALERT-SMS-PHONE` / `ALERT-VOICE-PHONE` at apply — do **not** reintroduce plaintext `alert_email` (or phone) Terraform variables.

## Keep the plan in sync

When you change scorecard dimensions/rubric, SLO targets, severity→channel mapping, alert secret names, or the monthly workflow contract, update `docs/plans/operational-excellence.md` in the same PR. Extend [rotate-secrets.md](docs/runbooks/rotate-secrets.md) when secret names change. After the living scorecard exists, update it (or let the monthly workflow commit do so) rather than only editing canvases.
